  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1: Possible record highs today and again Friday.\n\nContinued upper ridging and lack of moisture will allow for \nafternoon high temps reaching values near 15 degrees above climo or \nmore. Several climate sites are currently forecast to break records \ntoday by several degrees. Temps should be limited a bit more with an \nincrease in cloud coverage and precip chances from a frontal \nboundary, then back well above normal for Friday afternoon ahead of \na cold front. A few locations could flirt with record highs by a few \ndegrees. See records and forecast below.\n\nKey Message 2: Frontal boundary provides shower/few storm chances \ntonight into Thursday.\n\nA switch to more zonal flow aloft advects an elongated moisture axis \nand corresponding frontal boundary in across the northern half or so \nof the CWA for Thursday. This will allow for the return of precip \nchances. It should primarily be scattered showers since instability \nshould be lacking.  \n\nKey Message 3: Strong front late Friday to bring blustery winds and \nmuch cooler temperatures going into the weekend.\n\nWe quickly transition out of the zonal flow with the approach of a \nhigh amplitude upper trough and sharp attendant sfc cold front late \nFriday into Saturday. Not expecting much in the form of storms with \nagain limited instability with this system and the greater chance of \nshowers looks to be in the west mountains. The main impacts from \nthis front will be enhanced gradient winds kicking in for Friday \nnight into Saturday morning and then some of the coldest air of the \nseason ushering in. It will definitely feel like a rollercoaster of \nchange as highs Saturday look to be mainly in the low 50s for much \nof the mountains and then upper 50s to low 60s for the Piedmont. \nSunday morning is going to have frost/freeze concerns for much of \nthe area with progged lows mainly in the upper 20s to low 30s for \nthe mountains and mid to upper 30s for the Piedmont. This could \nagain be the case for Monday morning as well.",
